  {
    "chapter": 2,
    "verse": 13,
    "sanskrit": "देहिनोऽस्मिन्यथा देहे कौमारं यौवनं जरा ।\nतथा देहान्तरप्राप्तिर्धीरस्तत्र न मुह्यति ॥ १३ ॥",
    "iast": "dehino ’smin yathā dehe kaumāraṁ yauvanaṁ jarā |\ntathā dehāntara-prāptir dhīras tatra na muhyati || 13 ||",
    "phonetic": "dehino smin yathaa dehe kaumaaram yauvanam jaraa |\ntathaa dehaantara-praaptir dheeras tatra na muhyati || 13 ||",
    "trans1905": "As the dweller in the body experienceth in the body childhood, youth, old age, so passeth he on to another body; the steadfast one grieveth not thereat.",
    "transModern": "Just as the embodied soul continuously passes in this body from childhood to youth to old age, it similarly passes into another body at death. The wise are not bewildered by this.",
