  {
    "chapter": 2,
    "verse": 14,
    "sanskrit": "मात्रास्पर्शास्तु कौन्तेय शीतोष्णसुखदुःखदाः ।\nआगमापायिनोऽनित्यास्तांस्तितिक्षस्व भारत ॥ १४ ॥",
    "iast": "mātrā-sparśās tu kaunteya śītoṣṇa-sukha-duḥkha-dāḥ |\nāgamāpāyino ’nityās tāṁs titikṣasva bhārata || 14 ||",
    "phonetic": "maatraa-sparshaas tu kaunteya sheetoshna-sukha-duhkha-daah |\naagamaapaayino nityaas taams titikshasva bhaarata || 14 ||",
    "trans1905": "The contacts of senses with their objects, O son of Kunti, giving cold and heat, pleasure and pain, they come and go, impermanent; endure them, O Bharata.",
    "transModern": "O son of Kunti, the contact between the senses and their objects gives rise to fleeting sensations of heat and cold, pleasure and pain. They come and go and are impermanent. Learn to endure them patiently, O descendant of Bharata.",
