  {
    "chapter": 2,
    "verse": 20,
    "sanskrit": "न जायते म्रियते वा कदाचिन्नायं भूत्वा भविता वा न भूयः ।\nअजो नित्यः शाश्वतोऽयं पुराणो न हन्यते हन्यमाने शरीरे ॥ २० ॥",
    "iast": "na jāyate mriyate vā kadācin nāyaṁ bhūtvā bhavitā vā na bhūyaḥ |\najo nityaḥ śāśvato ’yaṁ purāṇo na hanyate hanyamāne śarīre || 20 ||",
    "phonetic": "na jaayate mriyate vaa kadaachin naayam bhootvaa bhavitaa vaa na bhooyah |\najo nityah shaashwato yam puraano na hanyate hanyamaane shareere || 20 ||",
    "trans1905": "He is not born, nor doth he die; nor, having been, ceaseth he any more to be; unborn, perpetual, eternal and ancient, he is not slain when the body is slaughtered.",
    "transModern": "For the soul there is never birth nor death at any time. He has not come to being, does not come into being, and will not cease to be. He is unborn, eternal, ever-existing, and primeval. He is not slain when the body is slain.",
