  {
    "chapter": 2,
    "verse": 47,
    "sanskrit": "कर्मण्येवाधिकारस्ते मा फलेषु कदाचन ।\nमा कर्मफलहेतुर्भूर्मा ते सङ्गोऽस्त्वकर्मणि ॥ ४७ ॥",
    "iast": "karmaṇy-evādhikāras te mā phaleṣu kadācana |\nmā karma-phala-hetur bhūr mā te saṅgo ’stv akarmaṇi || 47 ||",
    "phonetic": "karmany-evaadhikaaras te maa phaleshu kadaachana |\nmaa karma-phala-hetur bhoor maa te sango stv akarmani || 47 ||",
    "trans1905": "Thy business is with the action only, never with its fruits; so let not the fruit of action be thy motive, nor be thou to inaction attached.",
    "transModern": "You have a right to perform your prescribed duties, but you are not entitled to the fruits of your actions. Never consider yourself the cause of results, nor be attached to inaction.",
